Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev

Today ~claude/.claude and ~claude/.claude.json both sit on lab-claude's
root dataset, so just clean destroys Claude's credentials, settings,
history, and config, and every rebuild starts from scratch.

Patch 1 nullfs-mounts /jails/data/lab-claude/dot-claude onto
~claude/.claude. Patch 2 sets CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/claude/.claude
in the claude user's login environment, which moves .claude.json into
the mounted dir.

On .claude.json, from reading the Claude Code 2.1.283 installed in the
jail:

- With CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR set, the global config is
  $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/.claude.json, and settings.json, .credentials.json,
  history, projects, and plugins all live in $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR too.
  Pointing it at ~/.claude changes only where .claude.json lives.
- Without the variable, a ~/.claude/.config.json is preferred over
  ~/.claude.json. That would work with no env var, but it is a legacy
  fallback, so I did not rely on it.
- I found nothing that breaks with .claude.json inside .claude/. Claude
  already writes its .claude.json backups to ~/.claude/backups. The
  device-keys file is always under ~/.claude, whatever the variable
  says, and that is still the mounted dir.

Operator steps before restarting the jail:

    doas mkdir -p /jails/data/lab-claude/dot-claude
    doas chown 15000:15000 /jails/data/lab-claude/dot-claude

To keep the current state, copy ~claude/.claude/ into it and
~claude/.claude.json to dot-claude/.claude.json.

Not tested: I cannot build or start jails from inside lab-claude. On a
fresh build the jail starts before its users exist, so exec.prepare
creates /home/claude as root. I expect pw useradd -m to chown the
existing directory to claude. Please check that /home/claude is owned
by claude after the first build.

Only lab-claude is changed. lab-claude-devel has the same layout and
can take the same change if you want it there.

